  "description": "While fleeing from debt collectors who were trying to sell him off as a concubine to a perverted nobleman, Ja-Eon was eventually driven to the edge of a cliff and fell off. Believed to be dead, Ja-Eon opened his eyes to find himself in an unfamiliar place. Before him stood a massive man over seven feet tall, his face and entire body covered in red scars. He was undoubtedly the man of legend known as a “ghost beast” rumored to drink tiger’s blood by day and devour humans by night. Ja-Eon tried to flee, desperate to return to his father, the temple attendant, who was waiting for him, but all he got in response was a single, unexpected remark from the man: “I’m going to make you my mate.”\n\n……What?\n\n *“Why do I always attract people like this?”*\n\nA dangerous and relentless cohabitation with the mysterious “ghostly creature” he met at the edge of a cliff begins!\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
